According to the National Vulnerability Database, GHSA-5rjg-fvgr-3xxf affects the setuptools Python package and can allow arbitrary code execution during package installation due to insufficient validation of installation inputs.

Reflection on Insights and Process:
This lab demonstrated how Software Bill of Materials (SBOMs) enhance transparency and assurance in the software supply chain by making third-party dependencies visible and auditable. Generating SBOMs with multiple tools showed that different detection methods and formats can lead to significantly different results, as Syft provided broad and detailed component coverage while Trivy produced a cleaner but more limited output due to dependency detection constraints. Using Grype to analyze the SBOM reinforced the principle of defense in depth by enabling early identification of known vulnerabilities, highlighting the value of integrating SBOM generation and vulnerability scanning into the software development lifecycle to support secure design and ongoing risk management.

